# Consolidate Code to Main

## References

- [Consolidation draft](/Users/ctavolazzi/Code/active/waft/.cursor/plans/consolidate_all_code_to_origin_main_19a90ef1.plan.md)
- [.gitignore](/Users/ctavolazzi/Code/active/waft/.gitignore)
- [Devlog](/Users/ctavolazzi/Code/active/waft/_work_efforts/devlog.md)

## Plan

1. Initialize tracking and documentation

- Start Empirica session and preflight to capture baseline.
- Create a new work effort under `/Users/ctavolazzi/Code/active/waft/_work_efforts/` for this consolidation.
- Add the plan entry to [Devlog](/Users/ctavolazzi/Code/active/waft/_work_efforts/devlog.md).

2. Run preflight safety checks (no commits yet)

- Secret scan modified and untracked files; note any exclusions.
- Review [.gitignore](/Users/ctavolazzi/Code/active/waft/.gitignore) for secrets and temp artifacts; update if needed.
- Check branch protection and remote connectivity to `origin`.
- Create and push a backup branch.
- Check submodule or nested repo status and verify disk space.

3. Consolidate local working tree into main

- Review untracked files and confirm which should be included.
- Stage safe files only (exclude `.env`, sessions, secrets).
- Create a single consolidation commit with a clear message.
- Verify `git status` clean and review commit diff.

4. Review and integrate remote branches

- For each remote branch, capture log and diff stats.
- Categorize: merge, review, skip; get user decision when unclear.
- Merge selected branches into `main`, resolve conflicts, run targeted tests (no `npm dev` or `npm build`).

5. Push or PR

- If `main` is protected, open a PR; otherwise push directly to `origin/main`.
- Verify `origin/main` reflects all merged changes.

6. Close out tracking

- Update the new work effort and [Devlog](/Users/ctavolazzi/Code/active/waft/_work_efforts/devlog.md) with outcomes, merges, tests, and any skipped items.
- Run Empirica postflight to capture learning.

## Verification commands

- `git status`
- `git diff --cached --stat`
- `git log origin/main..main --oneline`
- `git submodule status`
- `git ls-remote origin`
- `df -h .`
